#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:1
msgid "Windows Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:3
msgid ""
"`cuda-oxide` supports `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` on Windows 10 22H2 and "
"Windows 11. For Linux, see [Installation](installation.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:6
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:8
msgid "NVIDIA GPU and a driver compatible with the installed CUDA Toolkit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:9
msgid ""
"[CUDA Toolkit 13.0+](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-installation-guide-"
"microsoft-windows/) (including `nvcc`, `libNVVM`, `nvJitLink`, and `cuRAND` "
"headers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:10
msgid ""
"Visual Studio 2022 or newer with MSVC x64 Build Tools, Windows SDK, and C++ "
"Clang tools (`libclang.dll` and `lld-link.exe`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:11
msgid ""
"Rust 1.99.1 (`x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`) with `rust-src`, `rustc-dev`, `rust-"
"analyzer`, `rustfmt`, `clippy`, and `llvm-tools`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:12
msgid "`libffi:x64-windows` installed via `vcpkg`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:14
msgid "Install the pinned Rust toolchain and components:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:16
msgid ""
"rustup toolchain install 1.99.1\n"
"rustup component add rust-src rustc-dev rust-analyzer rustfmt clippy llvm-"
"tools --toolchain 1.99.1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:21
msgid "CUDA and LLVM Environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:23
msgid ""
"Point `CUDA_PATH` / `CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH` at your installed CUDA Toolkit and "
"`LIBCLANG_PATH` at your LLVM/Clang `bin` directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:25
msgid ""
"$env:CUDA_PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\NVIDIA GPU Computing "
"Toolkit\\CUDA\\v13.2\"\n"
"$env:CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH = $env:CUDA_PATH\n"
"$env:LIBCLANG_PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\LLVM\\bin\"\n"
"$env:PATH = \"$env:CUDA_PATH\\bin\\x64;$env:CUDA_PATH\\bin;"
"$env:LIBCLANG_PATH;$env:PATH\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:32
msgid "Build from Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:34
msgid ""
"Open a Developer PowerShell for VS 2022 (x64) and install `libffi:x64-"
"windows` with `vcpkg`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:36
msgid ""
"$env:VCPKG_ROOT = \"C:\\vcpkg\"\n"
"& \"$env:VCPKG_ROOT\\vcpkg.exe\" install libffi:x64-windows\n"
"cd cuda-oxide\n"
"cargo install --locked --path crates/cargo-oxide\n"
"cargo oxide setup\n"
"cargo oxide doctor\n"
"cargo oxide run vecadd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:46
msgid ""
"For a build-only check without a GPU, run `scripts/smoketest.ps1 -BuildOnly` "
"from `cuda-oxide/`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:48
msgid ".\\scripts\\smoketest.ps1 -BuildOnly\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:52
msgid "Compute Sanitizer on Windows (WDDM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:54
msgid ""
"When running `cargo oxide sanitize` on a Windows GPU using the WDDM driver "
"model, enable the WDDM debugger interface once from an elevated "
"Administrator prompt:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/windows.md:56
msgid "& \"$env:CUDA_PATH\\compute-sanitizer\\EnableDebuggerInterface.bat\"\n"
msgstr ""
